EXT. LIFE RAFT - OPEN OCEAN - DAY

A yellow raft on flat grey water. A torn canopy flaps. The horizon is empty.

Five survivors share the space.

LEILA ACHEBE-KOWALCZYK, 30s, ties a rag to an oar. ANSELM ODUYA-FENWICK, 40s, bails with a cut-off bottle. SOLENE BRZEZINSKI-OKORO, 20s, hugs her knees. Old CAPTAIN ELWOOD NNAMDI-LINDQVIST, 60s, fingers a rosary. And little KIT ADEBAYO-HART, 12, lies curled in the middle.

LEILA
Eight days.

ANSELM
Nine.

LEILA
Eight.

ANSELM
She counted the first night as one.

SOLENE
I didn't count.

ELWOOD
Nine, then.

Anselm bails. Water arcs over the side. No one speaks.

KIT
(whisper)
Is it going to rain?

SOLENE
No.

KIT
How do you know?

SOLENE
I don't.

LEILA
Don't tell him that.

ANSELM
Why not? It's true.

LEILA
Because he's twelve.

Elwood turns a bead. Mouths a word. Solene watches the rosary as if it might answer.

SOLENE
Captain. Are we drifting?

ELWOOD
North.

SOLENE
Towards what?

ELWOOD
Towards nothing.

Anselm stops bailing. Stares at the water.

ANSELM
There's a shadow.

LEILA
Where?

ANSELM
Under us.

They all lean. A long dark shape slides beneath the raft, then another. Leila grips Kit's shoulder. Anselm lifts the bottle like a weapon. Elwood closes his eyes.

SOLENE
(whisper)
Don't look.

KIT
Why?

SOLENE
Because it looks back.

The shapes pass. Water laps. The raft rocks, gently, and settles.

LEILA
Dolphins.

ANSELM
Sharks.

LEILA
Dolphins, Anselm.

ANSELM
Fine. Dolphins.

Kit laughs, small, cracked. Elwood opens his eyes and looks at the sky, where a thin line of cloud has appeared in the east.
